  data: {
    LLM: "Player to dealer's right leads. Follow suit and overtake or trump as in partnership Tute. After winning a trick, a player may sing one 20 or 40 (king-horse of same suit); 40 in trumps before any 20. Trump 7 or 2 may be exchanged for the turned card before first trick. Winner is the player with most points; chip payments: 100 from each opponent if winner has 100 or fewer, 200 if 101 or more; 40 or 20 chips per declaration.",
    Player: "Player to dealer's right leads. Follow suit and overtake or trump as in partnership Tute. After winning a trick, a player may sing one 20 or 40 (king-horse of same suit); 40 in trumps before any 20. Trump 7 or 2 may be exchanged for the turned card before first trick. Winner is the player with most points; chip payments: 100 from each opponent if winner has 100 or fewer, 200 if 101 or more; 40 or 20 chips per declaration.",
    objective: 'Score the most points from card values in tricks, singing (king-horse 20/40), and last trick (10). Declaring tute (four kings or four horses) after winning a trick wins the hand outright.',
